<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Sagaing Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1315 CE – 1364 CE · capital Sagaing</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A breakaway Burmese kingdom on the west bank of the Irrawaddy that rivalled Pinya for half a century in the 14th century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1315 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saw-yun">Saw Yun</a>, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thihathu">Thihathu</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/pinya-kingdom">Pinya Kingdom</a>, quarrelled with his father and set up his own court at Sagaing, across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/irrawaddy-river">Irrawaddy</a> from present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandalay">Mandalay</a>. After Thihathu's death he gained control of the lands north and west of the river, and Pinya recognised Sagaing's independence.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Sagaing controlled the Mu valley <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> lands and routes toward the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chindwin-river">Chindwin</a> and the northern Shan states. Its kings kept up Pagan-style Buddhist patronage and court ceremonial, and the hills of Sagaing began their long history as a monastic centre. Court politics were turbulent, with regents and queens shaping successions.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1364 Shan forces of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mong-mao">Mong Mao</a> sacked Sagaing and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/pinya-kingdom">Pinya</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thado-minbya">Thado Minbya</a>, a Sagaing prince, seized power, executed rivals and in 1365 founded the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ava-kingdom">Ava Kingdom</a>, uniting the two rival courts. Sagaing later served briefly as a royal capital under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/konbaung-dynasty">Konbaung dynasty</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sagaing-kingdom.jpg" alt="Sagaing Kingdom" width="320" height="634"><figcaption>Image: Hybernator · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Burma_c._1350.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a>